# How to bake Telegram API credentials into the Nix package wrapper.
#
# Get them from https://my.telegram.org -> API development tools.
#
# Export the vars in your shell, then build with --impure so builtins.getEnv
# can read them. The wrapper sets them in the app's environment at runtime so
# it boots straight to the phone-login screen without any per-user
# credentials.toml setup:
#
#   export PALOMA_API_ID=123456
#   export PALOMA_API_HASH=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
#   nix build --impure
#
# Without the env vars (plain `nix build`) the build still succeeds; the app
# then falls back to ~/.config/paloma/credentials.toml at runtime.
#
# This file is documentation only — nothing imports it.
